# ELECTRICAL FIRE WITH SMOKE on the ground (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decisions 2026-10-23 and 2026-10-27): the heading, every item, action and sub-heading as printed (the printed gap in "If  the Engine Is Running" is a single space here). The row marks are the letters A to F of the AFM page that was compared. ASSUMPTION for the owner: the booklet may print numbers 1 to 6 instead; the marks are plain data (the `number` fields), so swapping them is one edit per row plus the typed table in tests/checklist-reference.ts. POWER lever Ground Idle (GI) is the lever position p0; FUEL valve OFF (lift and turn) is the state off of the FUEL selector (the lift is not modelled); Door is graded on the door release lever (state open); the printed row "Airplane evacuate immediately" has no panel action and stays a line. All other text is own wording. The smoke source, the outcome threshold and hold time, the onset window and the two causes are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-fire-ground
title: ELEC FIRE GROUND
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03-30 ELECTRICAL FIRE WITH SMOKE ON GROUND
  verified: "2026-10-27"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: parked
briefing:
  situation: "You are on the apron when you smell burning plastic and smoke fills the cabin. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The smoke is getting thicker and its source seems to be electrical."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p25
    lv.parking_brake: set
  quantities:
    airspeed_kt: 0
    smoke_density: 40
# ground_roll with the parking brake set: the aircraft stands, the PFD speed reads 0 knots (the brake holds it although the engine runs).
parameters:
  smoke_source: 1
  ground_roll: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: Electrical Fire with Smoke on Ground
procedure[8]:
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: A
        text: ELECT. MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: If the Engine Is Running
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_idle
        severity: critical
        number: B
        text: POWER lever
        action: Ground Idle (GI)
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.power
          is: p0
  - kind: group
    id: grp_eng_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: C
        text: ENGINE MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_fuel_valve
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: D
        text: FUEL valve
        action: OFF (lift and turn)
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: When the Engine Has Stopped
  - kind: group
    id: grp_door
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: door_open
        severity: critical
        number: E
        text: Door
        action: open
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: F
    text: Airplane
    action: evacuate immediately
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the cabin stays full of smoke; the density and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: cabin_smoke_full
    text: Cabin full of smoke
    hold_s: 30
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: smoke_density
      op: gte
      value: 95
# The two situations behind the one checklist: the engine is running, so the shutdown rows apply; or it has stopped already (ENGINE MASTER off from the start), so only the ELECT. MASTER and Door rows apply. The weights and the cause texts are instructor-review values.
variants[2]:
  - id: engine_running
    weight: 70
    applies[5]: elect_master_off,power_idle,engine_master_off,fuel_valve_off,door_open
    debrief: The engine was running, so the shutdown rows applied after the electrical master.
  - id: engine_stopped
    weight: 30
    controls:
      sw.engine_master: "off"
    applies[2]: elect_master_off,door_open
    debrief: The engine had stopped already, so only the electrical master and the door applied.
# The smoke of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
# The smoke shows over the panel, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that it shows within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  quantities:
    airspeed_kt: 0
  cues[1]: cabin_smoke
